        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.088,
            0.845,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** This quadrilateral is a parallelogram. In $\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C }$ and $\\Delta  ACD , AB = CD$ B $\\mathsf { C } = \\mathrm { A D }$ and $AC = AC.\\; \\mathrm{SO}_{2}$ by SSS congruence $\\Delta  ABC  \\cong \\Delta  CDA$ Therefore $\\angle 1 = \\angle 4$ and $\\angle 2 = \\angle 3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.163,
            0.582,
            0.295
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_37_image_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.313,
            0.706,
            0.352
          ],
          "content": "$\\angle 1$ and $\\angle 4$ are the alternate angles of AB and CD. So $\\mathrm { A B } { \\big \\| } \\mathrm { C D }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.353,
            0.725,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": "And $\\angle 3$ and $\\angle 2$ are the alternate angles of BC & AD So $\\mathrm { B C } { \\big \\| } \\mathrm { A D } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.393,
            0.71,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": "Thus both the pairs of opposite sides are parallel. Hence ABCD is a parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.442,
            0.847,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": "10. Will the sum of the angles in a quadrilateral such as the following one also be $3 6 0 ^ { \\circ } ?$ Find the answer using geometric reasoning as well as by constructing this figure and measuring."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.384,
            0.498,
            0.6,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_37_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.67,
            0.664,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Yes, the sum of angles in a quadrilateral ADCB is 360°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.71,
            0.624,
            0.75
          ],
          "content": "Join BD, Now Sum of angles of $\\Delta  ADB = 180^{\\circ}$ And sum of angles of $\\Delta \\mathrm{BDC} = 180^{\\circ}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.662,
            0.619,
            0.844,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_37_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.75,
            0.663,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": "Adding both sums of angles of quadrilateral $= 3 6 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.779,
            0.845,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": "11. State whether the following statements are true or false. Justify your answers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.822,
            0.845,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": "(i) A quadrilateral whose diagonals are equal and bisect each other must be a square."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.864,
            0.845,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": "(ii) A quadrilateral having three right angles must be a rectangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.927,
            0.131,
            0.941
          ],
          "content": "8"
